&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Remote - United States (Open to applicants located anywhere within the United States)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fueled is a leading digital strategy, design, and engineering agency. United with 10up – now the brand of our WordPress practice – we are a 300+ person team that has designed and built hundreds of digital products and experiences for brands like Google, Apple, The New York Times, ESPN, Victoria’s Secret, MGM Resorts, Albertsons, and CLEAR.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Front-End Web Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; at Fueled, you will provide critical technical support and consultation to clients and internal teams across a wide array of web properties. While you will be a versatile problem-solver who can navigate the broader WordPress ecosystem, we expect you to be an authority on front-end technologies (HTML, CSS, JavaScript, React) and thrive in a fast-paced, multi-project support environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Intentionally remote and globally distributed across six continents, our team thrives in a culture that values flexibility, creativity, and cutting-edge technology. Together, we’re shaping the future of digital experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you will do:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provide front-line technical support:&lt;/strong&gt; Actively monitor and respond to client support tickets, triage bugs, clarify UI/UX requirements, and maintain strong, empathetic live communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support diverse, high-volume projects:&lt;/strong&gt; Work across a large portfolio of concurrent client projects. You will frequently switch contexts throughout the day to resolve varying support requests, implement quick fixes, and push feature updates without sacrificing quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop and maintain enterprise front-ends:&lt;/strong&gt; Update, and maintain complex WordPress themes and custom Gutenberg blocks using React.js, modern CSS, and JavaScript.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enhance UI/UX and legacy interfaces:&lt;/strong&gt; Debug cross-browser issues, improve responsive design and accessibility on legacy systems, and ensure seamless visual integration across multiple client sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support &amp;amp; shape our product offerings:&lt;/strong&gt; Help maintain and enhance the user interfaces and front-end integration of our public product offerings like &lt;a href=&quot;http://ElasticPress.io&quot;&gt;ElasticPress.io&lt;/a&gt; and SiteWatch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you will achieve:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver timely resolutions:&lt;/strong&gt; Resolve front-end support tickets and deliver enterprise WordPress updates on schedule, maintaining exceptional client satisfaction through rapid and reliable issue resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maintain high-quality standards:&lt;/strong&gt; Write scalable, accessible, and responsive front-end code that meets our clients&#39; expectations as well as our engineering best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive client retention:&lt;/strong&gt; Contribute to the team, client, and overall company&#39;s success by providing exceptional customer relations and ensuring clients feel supported and heard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Triage and problem-solve:&lt;/strong&gt; Utilize critical thinking to accurately assess the severity of incoming tickets, prioritize workloads, and ensure our clients&#39; needs are met with the proper technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advance product UX:&lt;/strong&gt; Improve the growth, adoption, and stability of &lt;a href=&quot;http://ElasticPress.io&quot;&gt;ElasticPress.io&lt;/a&gt; and SiteWatch by ensuring a flawless front-end experience for our users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About you:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are an effective communicator.&lt;/strong&gt; You excel at explaining technical front-end concepts in client-friendly terms, possess strong empathy for user issues, and thrive in written client interactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are a front-end WordPress pro.&lt;/strong&gt; You are highly experienced with modern CSS, JavaScript, React.js, and Gutenberg block development, with a solid foundational understanding of PHP to navigate WordPress architectures safely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are an effective problem solver.&lt;/strong&gt; You are highly skilled at debugging UI glitches, resolving CSS/JS conflicts, optimizing legacy theme codebases, and ensuring cross-browser compatibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are adaptable and hyper-organized.&lt;/strong&gt; You are comfortable managing a high workload and a ticketing queue, effortlessly switching contexts between 5–10 different client projects in a single day, and delivering high-quality work under varying demands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are a self-starter and ongoing learner.&lt;/strong&gt; You are eager to tackle emerging front-end technologies, modern accessibility standards, and AI tooling, applying this knowledge to solve practical client challenges efficiently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
